    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nWe can use the skip parameter in vim.fs.dir to ignore some directories like .git and node_modules to avoid showing files inside those directories. Are you open to the idea of making this configurable in the config also ? I can also open a pull request if you want I already have a working version of this in my local config.",
